0.1.0 (2026-11-25):
- Variable scope: global or flow (new nodes: global, existing nodes keep flow) + context stores
- State in the variable is plain JSON (the timer stays inside the node) – works with global scope
  and persistent context stores
- Fixed: timers kept running after a redeploy
- Fixed: count time and interval were compared as text ("9000" > "60000")
- "kill" ends at once (end + waiting) instead of on the next tick
- Live preview of times in the dialog (e.g. 60000 ms = 1 min)
- New modern edit dialog (sections, live summary, spinners, validation), palette category "AFYA",
  Font Awesome icon, English UI with English + Polish help
- Short, consistent node status (value · time)
- MIT license, Node-RED >= 3.0, Node.js >= 18, unit tests (`npm test`)

0.0.5:
today I found that the reset /resetall function adds time indefinitely, which was not intended, from now on the reset function only adds the scheduled time to the time of the function call; for compatibility I added the addtime function
0.0.4:
kill & destroy messages in payload added
